   371	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   372	    """
   373	    Reassemble scattered fragments into a dense rectangle that is mirror-symmetric across both axes.
   374	
   375	    Input structure:
   376	    - The dominant color is background; every other monochrome 4-connected component is a puzzle piece.
   377	    - One 1-2-part frame group already sits in-place as a dual-symmetric outline of the target rectangle.
   378	    - The remaining small fragments are scattered elsewhere, and any non-frame fragment may have been quarter-turned.
   379	
   380	    Rule:
   381	    - Infer the portrait output dimensions from the total non-background area.
   382	    - Lock the frame group into its output-relative cells, keep only rotation-safe anchor inference from corner singletons,
   383	      then place all remaining pieces while trying every unique 0/90/180/270 orientation.
   384	    - The completed board must satisfy both left-right and up-down symmetry, and separate pieces of the same color may not
   385	      become 4-connected after assembly.
   386	
   387	    Key insight:
   388	    - The search is only manageable if rotation and symmetry are fused: each candidate pose must be checked against the
   389	      whole four-way reflection orbit, so the stronger D4 constraint cancels much of the extra branching introduced by the
   390	      larger piece count and the new quarter-turn freedom.
